@article{Sabatier.1998,
 abstract = {The advocacy coalition framework (ACF) has generated considerable interest among European policy scholars. This article summarizes some of the more important findings concerning, and changes to, the ACF since the last major erevision in 1993. These include (1) a much clearer model of the individual; (2) a clearer, more integrated concept of 'policy subsystem'; (3) much greater attention to the problematic nature of collective behavior among people who share policy beliefs; and (4) some sugestions concerning methods of ascertaining the existence and membership of advocacy coalitions. The article also briefly addresses the ACF's applicability to parliamentary systems, to the countries of Eastern Europe, and to the dynamic politics of the European Union.

nur sehr wenig Aussagen zur EU und einer m{\"o}glichen Anwendung des A-C-A dort. Elaboriert im Wesentlichen Sabatier 1993; nur interessant, wenn man sich n{\"a}her mit den Advocacy-Coalition-Ansatz besch{\"a}ftigen m{\"o}chte.},
